---
import PhaseLayout from '../../layouts/PhaseLayout.astro';
---

<PhaseLayout title="Quantum Computing Phase 3 — Polymath.Sys" activeNav="courses">

<style>
  .cpn { display:flex; gap:0; margin-bottom:2.5rem; border:1px solid #222; width:fit-content; }
  .cpn-link { font-family:monospace; font-size:11px; letter-spacing:0.08em; text-transform:uppercase; padding:0.45rem 1.1rem; color:#555; text-decoration:none; border-right:1px solid #222; }
  .cpn-link:last-child { border-right:none; }
  .cpn-link.active { background:#111; color:#fff; }
  .cpn-link:hover:not(.active) { background:#f3f3f3; color:#111; }
  .cpn-back { display:inline-block; font-family:monospace; font-size:11px; color:#888; text-decoration:none; margin-bottom:1.2rem; letter-spacing:0.05em; }
  .cpn-back:hover { color:#111; }
</style>

  <a href="/courses/quantum-computing" class="cpn-back">&larr; Quantum Computing Overview</a>
  <div class="cpn">
    <a href="/courses/qc-phase-1" class="cpn-link">Phase 1</a>
    <a href="/courses/qc-phase-2" class="cpn-link">Phase 2</a>
    <a href="/courses/qc-phase-3" class="cpn-link active">Phase 3</a>
  </div>

  <div class="track-header">
    <div class="track-badge badge-ai">Phase 3 &middot; Months 9-12 &middot; ~50h</div>
    <div class="track-title">Phase 3 &mdash; Variational Algorithms</div>
    <div class="track-sub">Explore the near-term frontier: VQE, QAOA, and quantum machine learning with PennyLane and Cirq. Understand what hybrid quantum-classical computation can achieve today and where the real research challenges lie.</div>
  </div>

    <!-- QC Step 4: VQE, QAOA, Near-term Algorithms -->
    <div class="step" id="qc3">
      <div class="step-head" onclick="tog('qc3')">
        <div class="step-num num-ai">4</div>
        <div class="step-info"><div class="step-title">Variational Algorithms &mdash; VQE, QAOA, quantum machine learning</div><div class="step-meta">Months 9-12 &middot; ~50 hours</div></div>
        <div class="step-arrow" id="a-qc3">&#9660;</div>
      </div>
      <div class="step-body" id="b-qc3">
        <div class="res-list">
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://pennylane.ai/qml/" target="_blank" class="res-link">PennyLane QML Tutorials (free) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">Xanadu's PennyLane has the best free tutorials for variational quantum algorithms and quantum machine learning. Covers VQE, QAOA, quantum classifiers, quantum GANs, and barren plateaus. Each tutorial has runnable code. PennyLane integrates with PyTorch and TensorFlow for hybrid quantum-classical models.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag must">Best for variational</span><span class="rtag tool">Interactive</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle><polygon points="10 8 16 12 10 16 10 8"></polygon></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://www.youtube.com/@qaboratory" target="_blank" class="res-link">Qiskit Global Summer School lectures (YouTube) <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">Annual free lecture series from IBM covering cutting-edge quantum computing topics. Past years include quantum simulation, quantum machine learning, and quantum error mitigation. High quality, research-level content from leading quantum scientists.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag vid">YouTube</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="res-item">
            <div class="res-icon"><svg class="res-svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M14.7 6.3a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.4l1.6 1.6a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l3.77-3.77a6 6 0 0 1-7.94 7.94l-6.91 6.91a2.12 2.12 0 0 1-3-3l6.91-6.91a6 6 0 0 1 7.94-7.94l-3.76 3.76z"></path></svg></div>
            <div class="res-content">
              <div class="res-name"><a href="https://quantumai.google/cirq" target="_blank" class="res-link">Google Cirq &mdash; quantum programming framework <span class="res-link-arrow">&nearr;</span></a></div>
              <div class="res-desc">Google's open-source quantum computing framework. Lower-level than Qiskit, giving you more control over circuit construction and noise simulation. The tutorials cover QAOA for MaxCut, VQE for molecular simulation, and running on Google's quantum processors. Learn both Qiskit and Cirq to be framework-agnostic.</div>
              <div class="res-tags"><span class="rtag free">Free</span><span class="rtag tool">Framework</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="insight"><b>The honest assessment:</b> Variational quantum algorithms are the most promising near-term approach, but barren plateaus and noise remain major challenges. Understand both the potential and the limitations. The researchers who make real progress are those who can clearly articulate what quantum computers CANNOT do, not just what they might do.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

</PhaseLayout>
